zB-ptwANlSnFSIu0OkFNC-mXkvlWFbS966LHlmdVFWnX43BHpI3QHfod6aplbXZUa9K_qgXU-N5Xk93L-DAr18a6HEhB7FGWeZxuQ5oMPI5DzREGlEcufoPVqIAwexRpI34MhASBTU-wMJPzhr:1wu1pc:CmqK7MKvnyJ4eo5crkoR3A68IkzM66QF7bPQSBDKvdY", "expire_date": "2026-08-26T05:48:52.575Z"}}, {"model": "sessions.session", "pk": "l18bpbtnzd7v9ugkxv0hufrkrpyulnly", "fields": {"session_data": ".eJxVjMsOwiAQRf-FtSED5VFcuvcbyAwwUjU0Ke3K-O_apAvd3nPOfYmI21rj1ssSpyzOQovT70aYHqXtIN-x3WaZ5rYuE8ldkQft8jrn8rwc7t9BxV6_taeCflAjkbLgguFk0VpUUJInHgkM56CBidkBGUM4ZEcECTVySCDeH_ySOQM:1vjbSP:H98bJs2kQTX-ldtFWEdlSMHnQylkGeUTIM5CXCRnutQ", "expire_date": "2026-02-07T11:05:33.559Z"}}, {"model": "books.author", "pk": 1, "fields": {"name": "Morgan Housel", "bio": "Morgan Housel is a partner at The Collaborative Fund. He is a two-time winner of the Best in Business Award from the Society of American Business Editors and Writers, winner of the New York Times Sidney Award, and a two-time finalist for the Gerald Loeb Award for Distinguished Business and Financial Journalism. He lives in Seattle with his wife and two kids."}}, {"model": "books.author", "pk": 2, "fields": {"name": "J.K. Rowling", "bio": "British author, best known for Harry Potter series"}}, {"model": "books.author", "pk": 3, "fields": {"name": "Thomas Mathew", "bio": "retired IAS officer, author, corporate strategist, defence analyst, and photographer"}}, {"model": "books.author", "pk": 4, "fields": {"name": "Joseph Murphy", "bio": "Irish-American New Thought minister and prolific author, famous for \"The Power of Your Subconscious Mind,\" who taught that positive thinking and belief in one's subconscious could transform lives, bridging spirituality, psychology, and self-help through widely read books, radio programs, and lectures"}}, {"model": "books.category", "pk": 1, "fields": {"name": "Psychology", "description": "The scientific study of the mind, brain, and behavior, aiming to understand and explain how people think, feel, and act, both individually and in groups, by exploring mental processes, emotions, development, and social influences"}}, {"model": "books.category", "pk": 2, "fields": {"name": "Fictional", "description": "creative, imaginative portrayal of characters, settings, events, or objects that do not exist in reality"}}, {"model": "books.category", "pk": 3, "fields": {"name": "Biographies", "description": "a non-fiction, detailed account of a person's life written by someone else, covering their experiences, character, and impact"}}, {"model": "books.book", "pk": 1, "fields": {"title": "The Psychology of Money", "category": 1, "isbn": "9390166268", "description": "TIMELESS LESSONS ON WEALTH, GREED, AND HAPPINESS\r\n\r\nDoing well with money isn’t necessarily about what you know. It’s about how you behave. And behavior is hard to teach, even to really smart people.\r\n\r\nHow to manage money, invest it, and make business decisions are typically considered to involve a lot of mathematical calculations, where data and formulae tell us exactly what to do. But in the real world, people don’t make financial decisions on a spreadsheet. They make them at the dinner table, or in a meeting room, where personal history, your unique view of the world, ego, pride, marketing, and odd incentives are scrambled together.\r\n\r\nIn The Psychology of Money, the author shares 19 short stories exploring the strange ways people think about money and teaches you how to make better sense of one of life’s most important matters.\r\n\r\nMORGAN HOUSEL is a partner at The Collaborative Fund and a former columnist at The Motley Fool and The Wall Street Journal. He is a twotime winner of the Best in Business Award from the Society of American Business Editors and Writers, winner of the New York Times Sidney Award, and a twotime finalist for the Gerald Loeb Award for distinguished Business and Financial Journalism.\r\n\r\n“Everyone should own a copy.”\r\n—JAMES CLEAR\r\nNew York Times Bestselling Author of Atomic Habits\r\n\r\n“Few people write about finance with the graceful clarity of Morgan Housel.”\r\n—DANIEL H. PINK\r\n#1 New York Times Bestselling Author of When, To Sell is Human, and Drive\r\n\r\n“Housel’s observations often hit the daily double: they say things that haven’t been said before, and they make sense.”\r\n—HOWARD MARKS\r\nCofounder and Cochairman, Oaktree Capital Management\r\n\r\n“That rare writer who can translate complex concepts into gripping, easytodigest narrative.”\r\n—ANNIE DUKE\r\nAuthor, Thinking in Bets", "full_text": "", "price": "339.00", "stock_quantity": 6, "cover_image": "book_covers/download.jfif", "publication_date": "2020-09-08", "publisher": "Jaico Publishing House", "pages": 252, "language": "English", "created_at": "2026-01-24T08:15:05.858Z", "updated_at": "2026-01-24T11:05:08.293Z", "authors": [1]}}, {"model": "books.book", "pk": 2, "fields": {"title": "Harry Potter 1–3 Box Set: A Magical Adventure Begins", "category": 2, "isbn": "1526620294", "description": "This collection from Bloomsbury Publishing is designed to pull new readers into the \"unforgettable, magical adventure\" from the moment Harry is left on the doorstep of Privet Drive. It is marketed as a collectible and perfect first step in any child's reading journey.", "full_text": "", "price": "385.00", "stock_quantity": 19, "cover_image": "book_covers/harrypotter.jfif", "publication_date": "2019-10-31", "publisher": "Bloomsbury Children's Books", "pages": 1216, "language": "English", "created_at": "2026-01-24T09:50:56.053Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-06T10:02:44.235Z", "authors": [2]}}, {"model": "books.book", "pk": 3, "fields": {"title": "Ratan Tata : A Life", "category": 3, "isbn": "978-935629569", "description": "Ratan Tata: A Life offers an intimate, well-researched biography of one of the modern era's most influential business leaders. The book follows the Tata Group's evolution—from its 19th-century trading roots to a global conglomerate—through Ratan Tata's leadership, principles, and steadfast ethics.", "full_text": "", "price": "893.00", "stock_quantity": 12, "cover_image": "book_covers/ratan_tata_life.jpg", "publication_date": "2024-10-25", "publisher": "HarperCollins India", "pages": 712, "language": "English", "created_at": "2026-01-24T10:02:10.999Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-02T14:56:45.987Z", "authors": [3]}}, {"model": "books.book", "pk": 4, "fields": {"title": "The Power of Your Subconscious Mind: Original Classic Edition | Premium Paperback", "category": 1, "isbn": "978-125023663", "description": "the infinite intelligence within your subconscious mind can reveal to you everything you need to know at every moment of time and point of space.", "full_text": "", "price": "349.00", "stock_quantity": 19, "cover_image": "book_covers/shopping_2.webp", "publication_date": "2015-02-01", "publisher": "St. Martins Essentials", "pages": 256, "language": "English", "created_at": "2026-01-24T10:18:05.655Z", "updated_at": "2026-01-24T11:18:23.262Z", "authors": [4]}}, {"model": "books.review", "pk": 1, "fields": {"book": 4, "user": 2, "rating": 5, "comment": "motivational book", "created_at": "2026-01-24T10:22:00.405Z"}}, {"model": "books.order", "pk": 7, "fields": {"user": 1, "created_at": "2026-08-06T10:02:44.219Z", "updated_at": "2026-08-06T10:02:44.219Z", "status": "pending", "total_amount": "385.00", "shipping_address": "Villupuram"}}, {"model": "books.orderitem", "pk": 7, "fields": {"order": 7, "book": 2, "quantity": 1, "price": "385.00"}}, {"model": "books.cart", "pk": 1, "fields": {"user": 1, "created_at": "2026-01-24T08:15:39.499Z", "updated_at": "2026-01-24T08:15:39.499Z"}}, {"model": "books.cart", "pk": 2, "fields": {"user": 2, "created_at": "2026-01-24T09:40:01.690Z", "updated_at": "2026-01-24T09:40:01.690Z"}}, {"model": "books.cart", "pk": 3, "fields": {"user": 3, "created_at": "2026-01-28T17:25:30.097Z", "updated_at": "2026-01-28T17:25:30.097Z"}}, {"model": "books.cartitem", "pk": 9, "fields": {"cart": 2, "book": 3, "quantity": 1}}]
